        "Content": "A Superb Five-Bedroom Detached Family Home No.14 Dun Ard, Craughwell, Co. Galway Eircode: H91 H5Y2 Guide Price: €490,000 \r\n\r\nSale Type: For Sale by Private Treaty \r\n\r\nJennifer Goggin of Keller Williams is delighted to bring to market No. 14 Dun Ard, a superb five-bedroom detached family home extending to approximately 195.46 sq. m (2,104 sq. ft.). \r\n\r\nBuilt in 2001 and presented in turnkey condition throughout, this impressive D1-rated residence (BER No. 109307140) offers generous and flexible accommodation in a highly convenient village location. Occupying an attractive position at the end of the row, the property enjoys an excellent sense of privacy and openness, with no house directly opposite. It is within easy walking distance of Craughwell Village and its wide range of everyday amenities. The location will appeal particularly to families and commuters. Craughwell Train Station is within walking distance, providing a convenient link to Galway City and beyond, while regular bus services also operate through the village. Craughwell National School is just a short distance away, making this an exceptionally convenient setting for family life. \r\n\r\nAccommodation \r\n\r\nUpon entering, you are welcomed into a spacious entrance hall. The generously proportioned sitting room features a fireplace and double doors leading through to a well-appointed dining room, creating a wonderful space for both everyday living and entertaining. Positioned to the rear of the property, the kitchen overlooks the beautifully maintained garden. A separate utility room provides valuable additional storage and practical workspace, together with direct access to the built-in garage. The garage offers excellent versatility and could be used for storage, a workshop, home gym, office or hobby room, depending on the purchaser’s requirements and subject to any necessary permissions. \r\n\r\nAlso located on the ground floor is a generous 1st bedroom, which could work equally well as a home office, playroom or additional reception room. A separate downstairs toilet completes the accommodation at this level. \r\n\r\nUpstairs, there are four well-proportioned bedrooms. Two of the bedrooms benefit from their own en-suite bathrooms, while the spacious master bedroom, positioned to the front of the house, also features a walk-in wardrobe. A main family bathroom serves the remaining bedrooms. Both en-suites and the family bathroom are fully tiled. \r\n\r\nExterior \r\n\r\nA standout feature of this exceptional home is its southwest-facing rear garden, which enjoys excellent afternoon and evening sunshine. Beautifully maintained, the garden incorporates a lawn and patio area, providing the perfect setting for outdoor dining, entertaining and family life. To the front, a well-maintained tarmac driveway provides generous off-street parking, complemented by a neatly laid lawn that creates an attractive and welcoming approach to the property. \r\n\r\nWith its generous proportions, excellent presentation, flexible accommodation, private end position, sunny southwest-facing garden and convenient location close to Craughwell Village, the train station, bus services and local school, No. 14 Dun Ard represents an outstanding opportunity to acquire a substantial family home. \r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this impressive property has to offer. To arrange a viewing, contact Jennifer Goggin on 087 2726025 or email jennifer.goggin@kwireland.com."
      },
